// the Herb Cottage, the Office and the Harbor Kitchen were drawn for the page as boxes, upright round things (lathes) and round
// blobs, every face painted by hand in code (no image: the owner's rule). This turns those pieces into the game's boxes as they are, so
// each catalog item looks as it did on the page: a page box becomes a sided box, a round thing or a blob a stack of thin slices (as
// pcLathe), a page colour (0xRRGGBB, a kind in its top byte: lit, a lamp's shade, fire) an [r,g,b] (lit ones never shaded). Heights:
// the page's walker was 1.86 of its units tall, the game's 50 art px, so a page unit of height is 27 art px; across, a page unit is a
// tile. Candle flames, the stove's fire and the drapes' hems move (24-pack-life: each piece's frames drawn once and kept).
