// ==== 23-w-dungeon-1-room.js (the game's, word for word)
// =====================================================================================
// THE DUNGEON, ITS LOOK (owner, 15 Oct 2026: "create a dungeon scene in the game, stand alone for now, walkable rotate, intricate detail
// ... very dark and moody, torches on wall, tiny mice scurrying, webs, skull, bones, cobblestone, dusting, musty ... start with 1 large
// room"): one large stone chamber of its own out in the blackness east of the laundry room (LBLD 'ldungeon', 21-world-map-5-land: off the
// map, the map tab's jump list takes you there), 12.8 by 10.8 inside and 130 art px high, the classic dungeon of a thousand games: a cell
// block's great room. Everything drawn by code in whole pixels, as the rest of the game (free pixel-art and voxel dungeons were the guide
// for what such a room holds and how it is shaped; nothing cut from any file). Here the room itself:
//   the walls: big rough blocks of grey-brown stone in staggered courses, each block its own shade, chipped, the mortar black; damp
//   streaks running down from the top, and the foot of every wall gone green with moss and mould, darker the lower; the barred slit of a
//   window high in the back wall (the night beyond it); an iron-banded oak door in the left wall, sealed, in a frame of dressed stone,
//   its grille dark; chains and shackles hung from rings; a prisoner's tally scratched in the right wall; soot up the wall over every
//   torch; cobwebs in the top corners; the mice's holes at the foot of the walls where their runs end (23-w-dungeon-2-things)
//   the floor: cobblestones, each stone rounded and its own shade, the joints black; damp patches, moss in the joints near the walls, a
//   drift of dust along every wall, straw and a few fallen bones; a rusted drain grate in the middle, where the floor dips
// Its things (torches, skulls, bones, barrels, the brazier, the gibbet, the mice) and the catalog's Dungeon department: 23-w-dungeon-2-things;
// the room set out and lit: 26-zzzzzzz-dungeon-placed. Its lights are its own (a low room: 42 gives it none): the torches', the brazier's, one
// faint cold fill so the far corners are not nothing.
